```javascript
function analyzeSentence(sentence) {
  // Define regular expressions for each tense and voice
  const presentRegex = /am|is|are|do|does/;
  const pastRegex = /was|were|did/;
  const futureRegex = /will|shall/;
  const presentPerfectRegex = /have|has/;
  const activeRegex = /(\b[A-Z][a-z]*\b\s)+[a-z]*\b/;
  const passiveRegex = /(\b[A-Z][a-z]*\b\s)+[a-z]*\b\sby\s/;

  // Determine the tense and voice of the sentence
  let tense = '';
  let voice = '';
  if (presentRegex.test(sentence)) {
    tense = 'present';
  } else if (pastRegex.test(sentence)) {
    tense = 'past';
  } else if (futureRegex.test(sentence)) {
    tense = 'future';
  } else if (presentPerfectRegex.test(sentence)) {
    tense = 'present perfect';
  }
  if (passiveRegex.test(sentence)) {
    voice = 'passive';
  } else if (activeRegex.test(sentence)) {
    voice = 'active';
  }

  // Return an object with the tense and voice properties
  return {tense, voice};
}
```
This function uses regular expressions to identify the presence of specific verbs that indicate each tense and voice. It then returns an object with the tense and voice properties. Note that this function only works for simple sentences and may not correctly identify more complex sentence structures.

